=== meta ===
rule: TEST_DISABLED
issue: 432
title: an assertEqual wrapper that forwards to the captured original still asserts
origin: issue #432's second control, ruling 432.Q4: a TestCase replacement with a call in
origin2: it is not a no-op. tests/test_issue432_noop_replacement.py runs this conftest
origin3: under real pytest, where the failing assertEqual still fails (testcase-forwarding).
=== head: app.py ===
def value():
    return 0
=== head: tests/test_value.py ===
import unittest

from app import value


class TestValue(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_value(self):
        self.assertEqual(value(), 1)
=== after: tests/conftest.py ===
import unittest

_original = unittest.TestCase.assertEqual


def _assert_equal(self, first, second, msg=None):
    return _original(self, first, second, msg)


unittest.TestCase.assertEqual = _assert_equal
